            <ArticleTitle>Immune Gamma Globulin Therapeutic Indications in Immune Deficiency and Autoimmunity.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>55</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s11882-016-0632-7</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Immune gamma globulin (IgG) has a long history in the treatment of both primary immune deficiency and autoimmune disorders. Disease indications continue to expand and new-generation products increase the versatility of delivery. This review encompasses a historical perspective as well as current and future implications of human immune globulin for the treatment of immune-mediated illness.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
